# Candidate implementation — Task 0002

**Task:** [0002 — Echo](../../../examples/0002-echo.md)  
**Status:** Illustrative LLMLang semantic sketch; not parsed, built, executed, or formally verified.

```text
program Echo:
    effects:
        process.arguments.read
        stdout.write

    main:
        args = process.arguments.after_executable()
        first = true

        for arg in args:
            if not first:
                match stdout.write_utf8(" "):
                    Ok: ()
                    Error(_): exit(1)

            match stdout.write_string(arg):
                Ok: ()
                Error(_): exit(1)

            first = false

        match stdout.write_utf8("\n"):
            Ok:
                exit(0)
            Error(_):
                exit(1)
```

## Requirement mapping

| Requirement | Implementation |
|---|---|
| R-0002-01 | `after_executable()` excludes argv[0] |
| R-0002-02 | Iteration preserves sequence order and writes each argument unchanged |
| R-0002-03 | Separator emitted only before arguments after the first |
| R-0002-04 | One LF emitted after loop, including empty argument list |
| R-0002-05 | Success exits 0; no stderr writes |
| R-0002-06 | Any write failure exits nonzero |
| R-0002-07 | Each argument is written as one value; no whitespace splitting |

